<title>USA: US Home Builders - Market Index falls to 53 in Sept.</title>
<headline>US Home Builders - Market Index falls to 53 in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Association of Home Builders said its Housing Market Index fell three points to 53 in October from 56 in September.</p>
<p>Builders' ratings of single-family home sales fell to 57 in October from 60 in September. Traffic of prospective buyers fell to 41 from 43. The component index for single family sales in the next 6 months fell to 60 from 62, it said.</p>
<p>A Housing Market Index over 50 generally means the number of positive responses received from builders exceeded the number of negative responses. The October index is based on the ratings of 210 respondents.  </p>
